  "title": "DayOne's Johor data centre project gets RM15 billion",
  "lede": "Seven banks — CIMB, Credit Agricole CIB, DBS, Maybank, OCBC, Standard Chartered and UOB — have formed a consortium to provide RM15 billion in financing for DayOne's data centre development in Johor, Malaysia. The deal ranks among the largest project financings in Malaysia's fast-growing data centre corridor. NTT Data Group is nearing an agreement with Anthropic to develop a large-scale data center in Osaka, with construction alone costing about ¥1 trillion (US$6.3 billion) and further investment expected for computing hardware, Nikkei Asia reports. The facility would support Anthropic's AI model training and inference workloads in Japan. Nvidia's share of China's data-centre AI chip market dropped to 34% in the first half of 2026, down sharply as US export controls restricted its product supply and domestic competitors led by Huawei captured share, according to an IDC report seen by Reuters. Chinese chipmakers are rapidly filling the gap left by restricted Nvidia GPUs.",
